│ patch_description        │ Replace Manhattan-distance wall targeting with true shortest-path distance on the current │
│                          │ passable grid.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing wall-selection logic can choose a wall-side standing square which is         │
│                          │ geometrically close but separated by already completed partitions. `get_bfs_move_char`    │
│                          │ then fails to find a route and returns `.`, causing repeated wasted turns and potentially │
│                          │ leaving partitions unfinished. Computing one BFS distance field per human decision makes  │
│                          │ unreachable candidates ineligible and selects the actually closest reachable              │
│                          │ wall-building position. The BFS also treats walls planned earlier in the same turn as     │
│                          │ blocked, consistently with simultaneous-action constraints.                               │
