│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ remove_redundant_boundary_walls                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current strategy intends to isolate the room into horizontal strips. However, it      │
│                          │ assigns each human many walls on the outer room boundary and on the left/right borders.   │
│                          │ These walls are redundant because squares outside the 30x30 room are already impassable,  │
│                          │ so adding walls along the perimeter cannot reduce pet reachability or improve the final   │
│                          │ connected components.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Those unnecessary assignments consume a large fraction of the 300 turns and delay         │
│                          │ completion of the only useful walls: the internal horizontal separators between strips.   │
│                          │ Assign only the two half-segments of each internal separator, preserving the existing     │
│                          │ split ownership between neighboring humans. This reduces total required walls from        │
│                          │ roughly 30(M+1)+60 to only 30(M-1), allowing partitions to close substantially earlier    │
│                          │ and giving pets less opportunity to cross between regions while construction is           │
│                          │ incomplete.                                                                               │
