│ patch_name               │ wall_aware_targeting                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace Manhattan-distance target selection with wall-aware BFS distances. As partitions  │
│                          │ grow, Manhattan distance frequently selects a wall-building stand square that is          │
│                          │ geometrically near but separated by an already completed barrier, causing humans to waste │
│                          │ turns or fail to reach their assigned boundary. Computing one BFS distance field per      │
│                          │ building human lets target evaluation use actual travel distance while respecting         │
│                          │ existing walls and walls scheduled by earlier humans on the same turn. This is a targeted │
│                          │ correction to the wall construction planner and also avoids choosing unreachable targets. │
