│ patch_name               │ strip_bfs_crossover                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover retains the higher-scoring current program’s efficient internal            │
│                          │ horizontal-strip partition plan, avoiding the lower-scoring border-wall construction from │
│                          │ the inspiration program.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It improves internal planning in two ways:                                                │
│                          │ 1. Each human computes one BFS distance field per turn, then uses exact reachable         │
│                          │ distances for selecting its next wall position instead of Manhattan distance. This avoids │
│                          │ selecting wall-adjacent standing squares that are geometrically close but cut off by      │
│                          │ already constructed partitions.                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Human move-target collision rejection is removed. Multiple humans are allowed to       │
│                          │ occupy the same square by the official rules, so rejecting those moves unnecessarily      │
│                          │ delayed construction.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The wall legality checks, tentative same-turn wall avoidance, pet-position tracking,      │
│                          │ simultaneous action model, and interactive I/O protocol are preserved.                    │
