│ patch_description        │ Assign horizontal strips to people according to their initial row order rather than input │
│                          │ order. The previous implementation assigned strip `i` to person `i`, although input       │
│                          │ person IDs are random with respect to position. Consequently, many people spent a         │
│                          │ substantial fraction of the 300 turns walking across the board before building their      │
│                          │ assigned half-walls.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change first reads every human position, sorts human indices by initial `(row,       │
│                          │ column)`, and assigns consecutive top-to-bottom strips according to that ordering.        │
│                          │ Actions still remain in original input order because `humans_global_state` is not         │
│                          │ reordered. This preserves protocol correctness while significantly reducing initial       │
│                          │ travel and allowing strip closures to complete earlier.                                   │
