│ patch_description        │ Humans are explicitly allowed to share squares, both initially after movement and while   │
│                          │ standing. The current planner incorrectly treats an already selected human move           │
│                          │ destination as forbidden for later humans, and later cancels such moves. This can         │
│                          │ unnecessarily stall people in narrow passages or near planned wall cells, delaying        │
│                          │ construction and occasionally leaving them on the wrong side of a partition.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Remove these artificial human-human movement conflicts while retaining the necessary      │
│                          │ check that a human may not move onto a square being made impassable in the same turn.     │
