╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_line_partitioner                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This approach replaces perimeter-strip construction with a dense horizontal partition     │
│                          │ strategy.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Humans are sorted by initial row and assigned two nearby horizontal barrier rows each.    │
│                          │ Building full-width barriers creates many narrow independent regions, which is much more  │
│                          │ favorable for the scoring function: smaller regions have a substantially higher           │
│                          │ probability of containing zero pets, avoiding the exponential `2^-n` penalty.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each human builds its first barrier while deliberately closing the final gap from the     │
│                          │ side of its second assigned barrier, ensuring it is not trapped away from its remaining   │
│                          │ work. For the final barrier, it evaluates both possible sides using a flood-fill estimate │
│                          │ of reachable area and contained pets, then closes from the better side. This is           │
│                          │ fundamentally different from the previous strategy of enclosing one large strip per       │
│                          │ human.                                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1042                                                                                   │
