│                          │ deterministic adaptive split. For each boundary, test split columns 8 through 22 and      │
│                          │ choose the one minimizing the larger estimated construction burden of its two neighboring │
│                          │ humans. The estimate includes segment length and lateral distance to the assigned         │
│                          │ segment.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the existing complete, non-overlapping partition layout, but gives a       │
│                          │ larger share of the left or right half to the neighboring person who starts closer to it. │
│                          │ It should reduce travel and make simultaneous boundary construction finish more reliably  │
│                          │ than always assigning exactly 15 cells per side.                                          │
